Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-21-2001||10:39 PM||||Got my '86SE V6(aka Bad#5) out of the garage finally today.  I replaced the radiator and thermostat and fired it up with a new battery(I put the Optima in my GT.) Whilst watching my temp guage, I smelled something burning... Not the coolant that I spilled, but like an electrical fire.  Sure enough, my alternator is flaming.  I shut the car off and the fire promptly dissapears(it was pretty small.)  So I get under the car and make sure nothing is loose, grounds are connected, etc...  I reconnect the battery and try it again.  Same results.  Anyhow, I swapped the Optima battery back in, and the car is fine!  Alternator charges fine, no fires, etc.  I put the other battery in the GT and watching it run for awhile with no problems... What the hell?||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||03-21-2001||10:43 PM||||What the hell? Very strange. Are you sure the battery was not connected backwards?||||reg||1
